/-!
# Carathéodory: a fixed index, cones, and points with directions

Mathlib has Carathéodory's theorem in the form `convexHull_eq_union`: every point of
`convexHull 𝕜 s` lies in the convex hull of an *affinely independent* finite subset. What it does
not have is any of the three things the theory needs — that `n + 1` points always suffice with a
*fixed* index type; the **conical** form, for the cone generated by a set; and the fact that the
convex hull of a compact set is compact.

**[rockafellar1970convex] Corollary 17.1.4**, and its companion 17.1.6, are **false as printed** and
are not formalised. Both assert that the positively homogeneous convex function generated by
`conv {fᵢ}` is computed by an infimum restricted to representations using at most `n` linearly
independent vectors. On `R¹` take `f₁(y) = -y` and `f₂(y) = y`: then `conv {f₁, f₂} ≡ -∞`, so the
generated function is `-∞` everywhere, while at `x = 1` the only admissible representations use a
single index and give the values `-1` and `1`. The elimination behind
`convFn_apply_affineIndependent` is unavailable, because an *affine* dependency has coefficients
summing to zero — so both signs carry a positive coefficient and the sign may be chosen by the cost
— whereas a *conical* dependency may have all coefficients of one sign. The printed proof passes to
"a minimal `α'` on the vertical line", which does not exist when the generated function is improper.

## Main results

* `mem_convexHull_iff_exists_fin_finrank_succ` — **Carathéodory's theorem** for points:
  membership in `convexHull ℝ S` is a convex combination indexed by `Fin (finrank ℝ E + 1)`.
* `exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_coneHull` — **Carathéodory for convex cones**: a point of the cone
  generated by `S` is a positive combination of a *linearly independent* subset of `S`. This is the
  algebraic core, the part a classical proof runs in `R^{n+1}`.
  `exists_card_le_finrank_of_mem_coneHull` is the same with the count `≤ n`.
* `exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull` — **Carathéodory for points *and
  directions***: a point of `conv P + cone D` uses at most `n + 1` generators in total, and their
  homogenisation is linearly independent. `exists_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull` forgets the
  independence, `exists_linearIndepOn_subset_liftPD` states it in the homogenised vocabulary, and
  `exists_finset_liftPD_eq` reads a finite subset of the homogenisation back as points and
  directions.
* `lift_mem_coneHull_liftPD` — the easy half of the homogenisation dictionary; it needs neither a
  norm nor finite dimension, and `HullDirections.lean` builds the converse half on it.
* `IsCompact.convexHull`, `Bornology.IsBounded.closure_convexHull` — the convex hull of
  a compact set is compact, and `cl (conv S) = conv (cl S)` for bounded `S`.
* `closedProperConvexFn_convHullFn_restrictFn` — the convex hull of a function with compact graph is
  a closed proper convex function.
* `exists_subset_linearIndepOn_of_sum`, `exists_subset_affineIndependent_of_sum` — the **indexed**
  elimination step: a representation `∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i` is thinned to a sub-*index set* on which
  the generators are linearly (resp. affinely) independent. The affine form carries a real cost
  `∑ i ∈ t, w i * c i` which the thinning is not allowed to increase.
* `exists_coalesced_sum` — Rockafellar's coalescing step: generators drawn from the same member of
  a family of convex sets are merged into their center of mass.
* `exists_affineIndependent_of_mem_convexHull_iUnion`,
  `exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_coneHull_iUnion` — the same counts for a union of convex sets, in
  the convex and the conical form; `exists_affineIndependent_of_convFn_lt`,
  `convFn_apply_affineIndependent` — the convex hull of a family of *functions*;
  `convHullFn_apply_fin` — the convex hull of a single function, on a fixed index.
* `inequalitySet`, `inequalitySet_subset_halfSpace_iff` — which closed half-spaces contain the
  solution set of a compact system of linear inequalities. The Lean statement carries `0 ∉ S`,
  which the usual statement omits and which is not removable; see the counterexample there.

## Implementation notes

The fixed index is what makes compactness available: with `Fin (n+1)`, `convexHull ℝ S` is the
image of a compact set under a continuous map, and compactness of the hull is one line.
Carathéodory's affinely independent subset has *at most* `n+1` elements, and padding it out to
exactly `n+1` is the only real work. The classical hypothesis for `cl (conv S) = conv (cl S)` is
boundedness, which coincides with compactness of the closure only because the space is
finite-dimensional. The conical Carathéodory
is an explicit induction on a cardinality bound rather than on a minimal representation, and its
conclusion asserts *strict* positivity of the coefficients, which is what lets `t.card ≤ finrank`
be read off from linear independence and makes the split into points and directions lossless.

## References

* [rockafellar1970convex] §17.
-/

open Set

namespace ConvexAnalysis

/-- A sum over `Fin N` of a family cut off after the first `m` indices is a sum over `Fin m`. This
is the padding lemma behind `mem_convexHull_iff_exists_fin_finrank_succ`. -/
theorem sum_ite_lt {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] {m N : ℕ} (h : m ≤ N) (g : Fin N → M) :
    ∑ i : Fin N, (if (i : ℕ) < m then g i else 0) = ∑ j : Fin m, g (Fin.castLE h j) := by
  classical
  rw [← Finset.sum_subset (Finset.subset_univ (Finset.univ.map (Fin.castLEEmb h)))]
  · rw [Finset.sum_map]
    refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => ?_
    have hlt : ((Fin.castLEEmb h j : Fin N) : ℕ) < m := j.2
    split
    · rfl
    · exact absurd hlt ‹_›
  · intro i _ hi
    have hnot : ¬ ((i : ℕ) < m) := fun hlt =>
      hi (Finset.mem_map.2 ⟨⟨i, hlt⟩, Finset.mem_univ _, by ext; rfl⟩)
    split
    · exact absurd ‹_› hnot
    · rfl

section Caratheodory

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]

/-- **Carathéodory's theorem** for points: a point of `convexHull ℝ S` is a convex combination of
`finrank ℝ E + 1` points of `S`, indexed by a *fixed* type. Repetitions and zero weights are
allowed, which is exactly what turns Carathéodory's "at most `n + 1` points" into a statement about
a fixed index. -/
theorem mem_convexHull_iff_exists_fin_finrank_succ {S : Set E} {x : E} :
    x ∈ convexHull ℝ S ↔ ∃ (w : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ)
      (z : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E), (∀ i, 0 ≤ w i) ∧ ∑ i, w i = 1 ∧
      (∀ i, z i ∈ S) ∧ ∑ i, w i • z i = x := by
  classical
  refine ⟨fun hx => ?_, fun ⟨w, z, hw₀, hw₁, hz, hx⟩ =>
    mem_convexHull_of_exists_fintype w z hw₀ hw₁ hz hx⟩
  rw [convexHull_eq_union] at hx
  simp only [Set.mem_iUnion] at hx
  obtain ⟨t, hts, hai, hxt⟩ := hx
  -- Carathéodory's subset has at most `finrank ℝ E + 1` elements
  have hcard : t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 := by
    have h₁ := hai.card_le_finrank_succ (k := ℝ)
    have h₂ : Module.finrank ℝ (vectorSpan ℝ (Set.range ((↑) : t → E)))
        ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E := Submodule.finrank_le _
    rw [Fintype.card_coe] at h₁
    omega
  -- its convex combination
  rw [Finset.convexHull_eq] at hxt
  obtain ⟨w, hw₀, hw₁, hwx⟩ := hxt
  rw [Finset.centerMass_eq_of_sum_1 _ _ hw₁] at hwx
  have htne : t.Nonempty := by
    rw [Finset.nonempty_iff_ne_empty]
    intro hcon
    rw [hcon, Finset.sum_empty] at hw₁
    exact zero_ne_one hw₁
  have hm0 : 0 < t.card := Finset.card_pos.2 htne
  -- pad the index set out to `Fin (finrank ℝ E + 1)`, repeating the last point with weight zero
  set r : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → Fin t.card :=
    fun i => ⟨min (i : ℕ) (t.card - 1), by omega⟩ with hr
  set zz : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E := fun i => ((t.equivFin.symm (r i) : E)) with hzz
  set ww : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ :=
    fun i => if (i : ℕ) < t.card then w (zz i) else 0 with hww
  have hrj : ∀ j : Fin t.card, r (Fin.castLE hcard j) = j := by
    intro j
    have hj := j.2
    refine Fin.ext ?_
    simp only [hr, Fin.val_castLE]
    omega
  have hmemt : ∀ i, zz i ∈ t := by
    intro i
    simpa only [hzz] using (t.equivFin.symm (r i)).2
  refine ⟨ww, zz, ?_, ?_, fun i => hts (hmemt i), ?_⟩
  · intro i
    simp only [hww]
    split
    · exact hw₀ _ (hmemt i)
    · exact le_rfl
  · have hstep : ∑ i, ww i = ∑ j : Fin t.card, w (zz (Fin.castLE hcard j)) := by
      simpa only [hww] using sum_ite_lt hcard fun i => w (zz i)
    rw [hstep]
    have hval : ∀ j : Fin t.card, zz (Fin.castLE hcard j) = ((t.equivFin.symm j : E)) := by
      intro j
      simp only [hzz, hrj j]
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [hval j],
      Fintype.sum_equiv t.equivFin.symm _ (fun y : {y // y ∈ t} => w (y : E)) fun _ => rfl,
      Finset.sum_coe_sort t w]
    exact hw₁
  · have hprod : ∀ i, ww i • zz i = if (i : ℕ) < t.card then w (zz i) • zz i else 0 := by
      intro i
      simp only [hww]
      split <;> simp
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => hprod i,
      sum_ite_lt hcard fun i => w (zz i) • zz i]
    have hval : ∀ j : Fin t.card, zz (Fin.castLE hcard j) = ((t.equivFin.symm j : E)) := by
      intro j
      simp only [hzz, hrj j]
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [hval j],
      Fintype.sum_equiv t.equivFin.symm _
        (fun y : {y // y ∈ t} => w (y : E) • (y : E)) fun _ => rfl,
      Finset.sum_coe_sort t fun y => w y • y]
    exact hwx

/-- **The convex hull of a compact set is compact**: it is the image of `Δⁿ × Sⁿ⁺¹` under
`(w, z) ↦ ∑ wᵢ zᵢ`, where `Δⁿ` is the standard simplex of weight vectors, the range of
`Convexity.StdSimplex.weights`. Mathlib has this only for *finite*
sets (`Set.Finite.isCompact_convexHull`). -/
theorem _root_.IsCompact.convexHull {S : Set E} (hS : IsCompact S) :
    IsCompact (convexHull ℝ S) := by
  classical
  set Δ : Set (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ) :=
    Set.range (fun t : Convexity.StdSimplex ℝ (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1)) =>
      (⇑t.weights : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ)) with hΔ
  have hΔmem : ∀ w : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ,
      w ∈ Δ ↔ (∀ i, 0 ≤ w i) ∧ ∑ i, w i = 1 := by
    intro w
    rw [hΔ, Convexity.StdSimplex.range_toFun_comp_weights]
    simp
  have hT : IsCompact (Δ ×ˢ (Set.univ.pi fun _ : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) => S)) :=
    IsCompact.prod (isCompact_range
      (Convexity.StdSimplex.isEmbedding_toFun_comp_weights ℝ _).continuous)
      (isCompact_univ_pi fun _ => hS)
  have hcont : Continuous fun p : (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ) ×
      (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E) => ∑ i, p.1 i • p.2 i :=
    continuous_finsetSum _ fun i _ =>
      ((continuous_apply i).comp continuous_fst).smul ((continuous_apply i).comp continuous_snd)
  have himg : _root_.convexHull ℝ S = (fun p : (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ) ×
      (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E) => ∑ i, p.1 i • p.2 i) ''
      (Δ ×ˢ (Set.univ.pi fun _ : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) => S)) := by
    ext x
    constructor
    · intro hx
      obtain ⟨w, z, hw₀, hw₁, hz, hwz⟩ := mem_convexHull_iff_exists_fin_finrank_succ.1 hx
      exact ⟨(w, z), ⟨(hΔmem w).2 ⟨fun i => hw₀ i, hw₁⟩, fun i _ => hz i⟩, hwz⟩
    · rintro ⟨⟨w, z⟩, ⟨hw, hz⟩, rfl⟩
      rw [hΔmem] at hw
      exact mem_convexHull_of_exists_fintype w z hw.1 hw.2 (fun i => hz i (Set.mem_univ i)) rfl
  rw [himg]
  exact IsCompact.image hT hcont

/-- **For a bounded set the closure and the convex hull commute.** -/
theorem _root_.Bornology.IsBounded.closure_convexHull {S : Set E} (hS : Bornology.IsBounded S) :
    closure (convexHull ℝ S) = convexHull ℝ (closure S) := by
  have hcl : IsCompact (closure S) :=
    Metric.isCompact_of_isClosed_isBounded isClosed_closure hS.closure
  refine subset_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · exact closure_minimal (convexHull_mono subset_closure)
      (IsCompact.isClosed (IsCompact.convexHull hcl))
  · exact convexHull_min (closure_mono (subset_convexHull ℝ S))
      (Convex.closure (convex_convexHull ℝ S))

end Caratheodory

/-! ### The convex hull of a function with compact graph -/

section GraphHull

open scoped Pointwise

variable (E : Type*) [NormedAddCommGroup E]

/-- The **upward vertical ray** `{0} × [0, ∞)` of `E × ℝ`: the set of directions in which every
epigraph recedes. -/
private def upRay : Set (E × ℝ) := {p : E × ℝ | p.1 = 0 ∧ 0 ≤ p.2}

variable {E} {S : Set E} {g : E → ℝ}

/-- The upward vertical ray is closed. -/
private theorem isClosed_upRay : IsClosed (upRay E) := by
  have hset : upRay E
      = (Prod.fst ⁻¹' ({0} : Set E)) ∩ (Prod.snd ⁻¹' (Set.Ici (0 : ℝ))) := rfl
  rw [hset]
  exact (isClosed_singleton.preimage continuous_fst).inter
    (isClosed_Ici.preimage continuous_snd)

/-- The epigraph of a function that is real-valued on `S` and `+∞` off `S` is the graph of that
function over `S`, translated upward along the vertical ray. -/
private theorem epi_restrictFn_eq (S : Set E) (g : E → ℝ) :
    epi (restrictFn S fun x => ((g x : ℝ) : EReal))
      = (fun x => ((x, g x) : E × ℝ)) '' S + upRay E := by
  ext p
  constructor
  · intro hp
    rw [mem_epi] at hp
    by_cases hp1 : p.1 ∈ S
    · rw [restrictFn_of_mem hp1, EReal.coe_le_coe_iff] at hp
      exact ⟨(p.1, g p.1), ⟨p.1, hp1, rfl⟩, (0, p.2 - g p.1), ⟨rfl, by linarith⟩,
        Prod.ext (by change p.1 + 0 = p.1; rw [add_zero])
          (by change g p.1 + (p.2 - g p.1) = p.2; ring)⟩
    · rw [restrictFn_of_notMem hp1] at hp
      exact absurd hp (by simp)
  · rintro ⟨u, ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩, v, ⟨hv1, hv2⟩, rfl⟩
    rw [mem_epi]
    have h1 : ((x, g x) + v).1 = x := by change x + v.1 = x; rw [hv1, add_zero]
    rw [h1, restrictFn_of_mem hx]
    change ((g x : ℝ) : EReal) ≤ ((g x + v.2 : ℝ) : EReal)
    exact_mod_cast le_add_of_nonneg_right hv2

variable [NormedSpace ℝ E]

/-- The upward vertical ray is convex. -/
private theorem convex_upRay : Convex ℝ (upRay E) := by
  rintro p ⟨hp1, hp2⟩ q ⟨hq1, hq2⟩ a b ha hb -
  refine ⟨?_, ?_⟩
  · change a • p.1 + b • q.1 = 0
    rw [hp1, hq1, smul_zero, smul_zero, add_zero]
  · change (0 : ℝ) ≤ a * p.2 + b * q.2
    exact add_nonneg (mul_nonneg ha hp2) (mul_nonneg hb hq2)

/-- Taking the convex hull of such an epigraph leaves the vertical ray alone: it acts only on the
graph. -/
private theorem convexHull_epi_restrictFn_eq (S : Set E) (g : E → ℝ) :
    convexHull ℝ (epi (restrictFn S fun x => ((g x : ℝ) : EReal)))
      = convexHull ℝ ((fun x => ((x, g x) : E × ℝ)) '' S) + upRay E := by
  rw [epi_restrictFn_eq, convexHull_add, (convex_upRay (E := E)).convexHull_eq]

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]

/-- **The convex hull of the epigraph of a function with compact graph is closed.** The graph is
compact, so its convex hull is compact, and a compact set plus the closed vertical ray is closed. -/
theorem isClosed_convexHull_epi_restrictFn (hS : IsCompact S) (hg : ContinuousOn g S) :
    IsClosed (convexHull ℝ (epi (restrictFn S fun x => ((g x : ℝ) : EReal)))) := by
  rw [convexHull_epi_restrictFn_eq]
  exact isClosed_upRay.add_left_of_isCompact (IsCompact.convexHull
    (hS.image_of_continuousOn (ContinuousOn.prodMk continuousOn_id hg)))

/-- **The convex hull of a function with compact graph is a closed proper convex function.** For
non-empty compact `S` and `g` continuous on `S`, extended by `+∞`, the graph `G` of `g` is
compact, so `conv G` is compact; `epi f = G + K` for the upward vertical ray
`K`, so `conv (epi f) = conv G + K` is closed and upward closed on each vertical line, hence *is*
an epigraph. -/
theorem closedProperConvexFn_convHullFn_restrictFn (hSne : S.Nonempty) (hS : IsCompact S)
    (hg : ContinuousOn g S) :
    ClosedProperConvexFn (convHullFn (restrictFn S fun x => ((g x : ℝ) : EReal))) := by
  set f : E → EReal := restrictFn S (fun x => ((g x : ℝ) : EReal)) with hfdef
  set G : Set (E × ℝ) := (fun x => ((x, g x) : E × ℝ)) '' S with hGdef
  have hGc : IsCompact G := hS.image_of_continuousOn (ContinuousOn.prodMk continuousOn_id hg)
  have hCc : IsCompact (convexHull ℝ G) := IsCompact.convexHull hGc
  have hFeq : convexHull ℝ (epi f) = convexHull ℝ G + upRay E := convexHull_epi_restrictFn_eq S g
  have hFcl : IsClosed (convexHull ℝ (epi f)) := isClosed_convexHull_epi_restrictFn hS hg
  have hEpi : IsEpiLike (convexHull ℝ (epi f)) := by
    refine IsEpiLike.of_isClosed (fun x μ ν hp hμν => ?_) hFcl
    rw [hFeq] at hp ⊢
    obtain ⟨c, hc, k, hk, hck⟩ := hp
    refine ⟨c, hc, k + (0, ν - μ), ⟨?_, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
    · change k.1 + 0 = 0
      rw [add_zero]
      exact hk.1
    · change (0 : ℝ) ≤ k.2 + (ν - μ)
      have := hk.2
      linarith
    · have hck' : c + k = (x, μ) := hck
      change c + (k + (0, ν - μ)) = (x, ν)
      rw [← add_assoc, hck']
      exact Prod.ext (by change x + 0 = x; rw [add_zero])
        (by change μ + (ν - μ) = ν; ring)
  obtain ⟨x₀, hx₀⟩ := hSne
  have hCne : (convexHull ℝ G).Nonempty := ⟨(x₀, g x₀), subset_convexHull ℝ G ⟨x₀, hx₀, rfl⟩⟩
  obtain ⟨q, -, hqmin⟩ := hCc.exists_isMinOn hCne continuous_snd.continuousOn
  have hproper : Proper (convHullFn f) := by
    refine ⟨⟨x₀, ?_⟩, fun x hbot => ?_⟩
    · rw [mem_dom]
      refine lt_of_le_of_lt (convHullFn_le f x₀) ?_
      rw [hfdef, restrictFn_of_mem hx₀]
      exact EReal.coe_lt_top _
    · have hge : ((q.2 : ℝ) : EReal) ≤ convHullFn f x := by
        refine le_ofEpi fun μ hμ => ?_
        rw [hFeq] at hμ
        obtain ⟨c, hc, k, hk, hck⟩ := hμ
        have h2 : c.2 + k.2 = μ := congrArg Prod.snd hck
        have hmin := isMinOn_iff.1 hqmin c hc
        have hk2 := hk.2
        exact_mod_cast (by linarith : q.2 ≤ μ)
      rw [hbot] at hge
      exact absurd (le_bot_iff.1 hge) (EReal.coe_ne_bot _)
  refine ClosedProperConvexFn.of_isClosed_epi (convexFn_convHullFn f) ?_ hproper
  have hepiF : epi (convHullFn f) = convexHull ℝ (epi f) := epi_ofEpi hEpi
  rw [hepiF]
  exact hFcl

end GraphHull

/-! ### Carathéodory for convex cones -/

section Cone

variable {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E]

/-- The engine of the conical form of Carathéodory's theorem, as an induction on a cardinality
bound: a conical representation over a linearly *dependent* finite set can be replaced by one over
a strictly smaller set, by subtracting a multiple of the dependency just large enough to drive one
positive coefficient to zero. -/
private theorem exists_linearIndepOn_coneRepr_aux {S : Set E} :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (t : Finset E), t.card ≤ n → ↑t ⊆ S → ∀ w : E → ℝ, (∀ y ∈ t, 0 < w y) →
      ∃ (t' : Finset E) (w' : E → ℝ), ↑t' ⊆ S ∧ (∀ y ∈ t', 0 < w' y) ∧
        LinearIndepOn ℝ id (t' : Set E) ∧ ∑ y ∈ t', w' y • y = ∑ y ∈ t, w y • y := by
  classical
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro t hcard hts w hw
    have ht : t = ∅ := Finset.card_eq_zero.1 (Nat.le_zero.1 hcard)
    subst ht
    exact ⟨∅, w, by simp, by simp, by simp, rfl⟩
  | succ n ih =>
    intro t hcard hts w hw
    by_cases hli : LinearIndepOn ℝ id (t : Set E)
    · exact ⟨t, w, hts, hw, hli, rfl⟩
    -- a non-trivial linear relation supported inside `t`
    obtain ⟨fr, hfsupp, hfsum, hfne⟩ := linearDepOn_iff.1 hli
    rw [Finsupp.mem_supported] at hfsupp
    simp only [id_eq] at hfsum
    have hsub : fr.support ⊆ t := by
      intro y hy
      exact_mod_cast hfsupp hy
    have hνsum : ∑ y ∈ t, fr y • y = 0 := by
      rw [← Finset.sum_subset hsub fun y _ hy => by
        rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.1 hy, zero_smul]]
      exact hfsum
    obtain ⟨y₂, hy₂⟩ := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.2 hfne
    have hy₂t : y₂ ∈ t := hsub hy₂
    have hy₂ne : fr y₂ ≠ 0 := Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hy₂
    -- normalise the relation so that one coefficient is strictly positive
    obtain ⟨mu, hmusum, y₀, hy₀t, hy₀pos⟩ :
        ∃ mu : E → ℝ, (∑ y ∈ t, mu y • y = 0) ∧ ∃ y₀ ∈ t, 0 < mu y₀ := by
      rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hy₂ne with hneg | hpos
      · refine ⟨fun y => -fr y, ?_, y₂, hy₂t, by linarith⟩
        simp only [neg_smul, Finset.sum_neg_distrib, hνsum, neg_zero]
      · exact ⟨fun y => fr y, hνsum, y₂, hy₂t, hpos⟩
    -- the largest multiple of the relation that keeps every coefficient non-negative
    set Pos : Finset E := t.filter (fun y => 0 < mu y) with hPosdef
    have hPosne : Pos.Nonempty := ⟨y₀, by simp [hPosdef, hy₀t, hy₀pos]⟩
    obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁Pos, hy₁min⟩ := Finset.exists_min_image Pos (fun y => w y / mu y) hPosne
    have hy₁t : y₁ ∈ t := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hy₁Pos).1
    have hy₁mu : 0 < mu y₁ := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hy₁Pos).2
    set lam : ℝ := w y₁ / mu y₁ with hlamdef
    have hlampos : 0 < lam := div_pos (hw y₁ hy₁t) hy₁mu
    set w' : E → ℝ := fun y => w y - lam * mu y with hw'def
    have hw'nonneg : ∀ y ∈ t, 0 ≤ w' y := by
      intro y hy
      by_cases hmy : 0 < mu y
      · have hmem : y ∈ Pos := by simp [hPosdef, hy, hmy]
        have hdiv := hy₁min y hmem
        have hmul : lam * mu y ≤ w y := (le_div_iff₀ hmy).1 hdiv
        simp only [hw'def]
        linarith
      · push Not at hmy
        have hle : lam * mu y ≤ 0 := mul_nonpos_of_nonneg_of_nonpos hlampos.le hmy
        have hwy := hw y hy
        simp only [hw'def]
        linarith
    have hw'y₁ : w' y₁ = 0 := by
      simp only [hw'def, hlamdef]
      rw [div_mul_cancel₀ _ hy₁mu.ne']
      ring
    have hsum' : ∑ y ∈ t, w' y • y = ∑ y ∈ t, w y • y := by
      have hsplit : ∑ y ∈ t, w' y • y
          = (∑ y ∈ t, w y • y) - lam • ∑ y ∈ t, mu y • y := by
        rw [Finset.smul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun y _ => ?_
        simp only [hw'def, sub_smul, smul_smul]
      rw [hsplit, hmusum, smul_zero, sub_zero]
    -- drop the coefficients that have become zero
    set t' : Finset E := t.filter (fun y => 0 < w' y) with ht'def
    have ht'sub : t' ⊆ t := Finset.filter_subset _ _
    have ht'pos : ∀ y ∈ t', 0 < w' y := fun y hy => (Finset.mem_filter.1 hy).2
    have ht'sum : ∑ y ∈ t', w' y • y = ∑ y ∈ t, w' y • y := by
      refine Finset.sum_subset ht'sub fun y hy hy' => ?_
      have hnp : ¬ (0 < w' y) := fun h => hy' (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hy, h⟩)
      have h0 : w' y = 0 := le_antisymm (not_lt.1 hnp) (hw'nonneg y hy)
      rw [h0, zero_smul]
    have hy₁notin : y₁ ∉ t' := by
      simp [ht'def, hw'y₁]
    have ht'card : t'.card ≤ n := by
      have hss : t' ⊆ t.erase y₁ := fun y hy =>
        Finset.mem_erase.2 ⟨fun h => hy₁notin (h ▸ hy), ht'sub hy⟩
      have h1 := Finset.card_le_card hss
      rw [Finset.card_erase_of_mem hy₁t] at h1
      have h2 : 0 < t.card := Finset.card_pos.2 ⟨y₁, hy₁t⟩
      omega
    obtain ⟨t'', w'', hts'', hpos'', hli'', hsum''⟩ :=
      ih t' ht'card (fun y hy => hts (ht'sub (by exact_mod_cast hy))) w' ht'pos
    exact ⟨t'', w'', hts'', hpos'', hli'', by rw [hsum'', ht'sum, hsum']⟩

/-- **Carathéodory's theorem for convex cones.** A point of the cone generated by `S` is a
non-negative combination of a *linearly independent* finite subset of `S`, with strictly positive
coefficients. This is the algebraic core of Carathéodory's theorem — the part a classical proof
carries out in `R^{n+1}` — and Mathlib covers only the convex hull. -/
theorem exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_coneHull {S : Set E} {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ S) :
    ∃ (t : Finset E) (w : E → ℝ), ↑t ⊆ S ∧ (∀ y ∈ t, 0 < w y) ∧
      LinearIndepOn ℝ id (t : Set E) ∧ ∑ y ∈ t, w y • y = x := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨c, hcs, hc0, hcx⟩ := PointedCone.mem_hull_set.1 hx
  have hpos : ∀ y ∈ c.support, 0 < c y := fun y hy =>
    lt_of_le_of_ne (hc0 y) (Ne.symm (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hy))
  obtain ⟨t, w, hts, hw, hli, hsum⟩ :=
    exists_linearIndepOn_coneRepr_aux c.support.card c.support le_rfl hcs c hpos
  exact ⟨t, w, hts, hw, hli, by rw [hsum]; exact hcx⟩

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]

/-- The conical Carathéodory bound: `n` generators suffice, where `n = dim E`. -/
theorem exists_card_le_finrank_of_mem_coneHull {S : Set E} {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ S) :
    ∃ (t : Finset E) (w : E → ℝ), ↑t ⊆ S ∧ (∀ y ∈ t, 0 < w y) ∧
      t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E ∧ ∑ y ∈ t, w y • y = x := by
  obtain ⟨t, w, hts, hw, hli, hsum⟩ := exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_coneHull hx
  exact ⟨t, w, hts, hw, LinearIndependent.finset_card_le_finrank hli, hsum⟩

end Cone

/-! ### Carathéodory for points and directions -/

section LiftPD

variable {E : Type*}

/-- The homogenisation of a set of points and directions: `P` is lifted to height `1` and `D` to
height `0` in `ℝ × E`. Rockafellar's `S'`. -/
def liftPD (P D : Set E) : Set (ℝ × E) :=
  (fun y : E => ((1 : ℝ), y)) '' P ∪ (fun y : E => ((0 : ℝ), y)) '' D

/-- A point of `P` sits at height `1` in `liftPD P D`. -/
theorem mem_liftPD_one {P D : Set E} {y : E} (hy : y ∈ P) :
    ((1 : ℝ), y) ∈ liftPD P D := Or.inl ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩

/-- A direction of `D` sits at height `0` in `liftPD P D`. -/
theorem mem_liftPD_zero {P D : Set E} {y : E} (hy : y ∈ D) :
    ((0 : ℝ), y) ∈ liftPD P D := Or.inr ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩

/-- Every element of `liftPD P D` sits at height `1` or at height `0`. -/
theorem fst_eq_or_of_mem_liftPD {P D : Set E} {q : ℝ × E} (hq : q ∈ liftPD P D) :
    q.1 = 1 ∨ q.1 = 0 := by
  rcases hq with ⟨y, _, rfl⟩ | ⟨y, _, rfl⟩
  · exact Or.inl rfl
  · exact Or.inr rfl

/-- An element of `liftPD P D` at height `1` is a point of `P`. -/
theorem mem_of_mem_liftPD_of_fst_eq_one {P D : Set E} {q : ℝ × E}
    (hq : q ∈ liftPD P D) (h1 : q.1 = 1) : q.2 ∈ P := by
  rcases hq with ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩ | ⟨y, _, rfl⟩
  · exact hy
  · exact absurd h1 (by norm_num)

/-- An element of `liftPD P D` at height `0` is a direction of `D`. -/
theorem mem_of_mem_liftPD_of_fst_eq_zero {P D : Set E} {q : ℝ × E}
    (hq : q ∈ liftPD P D) (h0 : q.1 = 0) : q.2 ∈ D := by
  rcases hq with ⟨y, _, rfl⟩ | ⟨y, hy, rfl⟩
  · exact absurd h0 (by norm_num)
  · exact hy

/-- **Splitting a finite subset of the homogenisation.** A finite set of vectors drawn from
`liftPD P D` is itself the homogenisation of a finite set of points of `P` and a finite set of
directions of `D`, with the two cardinalities adding up to its own. -/
theorem exists_finset_liftPD_eq {P D : Set E} {t : Finset (ℝ × E)} (ht : ↑t ⊆ liftPD P D) :
    ∃ p d : Finset E, ↑p ⊆ P ∧ ↑d ⊆ D ∧ p.card + d.card = t.card ∧
      liftPD (↑p) (↑d) = (↑t : Set (ℝ × E)) := by
  classical
  set t₁ : Finset (ℝ × E) := t.filter (fun q => q.1 = 1) with ht₁def
  set t₀ : Finset (ℝ × E) := t.filter (fun q => q.1 = 0) with ht₀def
  have ht01 : ∀ q ∈ t, q.1 = 1 ∨ q.1 = 0 := fun q hq =>
    fst_eq_or_of_mem_liftPD (ht (Finset.mem_coe.2 hq))
  have heq₁ : ∀ q ∈ t₁, ((1 : ℝ), q.2) = q := fun q hq =>
    Prod.ext (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2.symm rfl
  have heq₀ : ∀ q ∈ t₀, ((0 : ℝ), q.2) = q := fun q hq =>
    Prod.ext (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2.symm rfl
  have hinj₁ : ∀ q ∈ t₁, ∀ q' ∈ t₁, q.2 = q'.2 → q = q' := by
    intro q hq q' hq' h
    exact Prod.ext (by rw [(Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2, (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq').2]) h
  have hinj₀ : ∀ q ∈ t₀, ∀ q' ∈ t₀, q.2 = q'.2 → q = q' := by
    intro q hq q' hq' h
    exact Prod.ext (by rw [(Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2, (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq').2]) h
  have hinjOn₁ : Set.InjOn Prod.snd (↑t₁ : Set (ℝ × E)) := fun q hq q' hq' h =>
    hinj₁ q (by exact_mod_cast hq) q' (by exact_mod_cast hq') h
  have hinjOn₀ : Set.InjOn Prod.snd (↑t₀ : Set (ℝ × E)) := fun q hq q' hq' h =>
    hinj₀ q (by exact_mod_cast hq) q' (by exact_mod_cast hq') h
  have hdisj : Disjoint t₁ t₀ := by
    rw [Finset.disjoint_left]
    intro q hq hq'
    have h1 := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2
    have h0 := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq').2
    rw [h1] at h0
    norm_num at h0
  have hunion : t₁ ∪ t₀ = t := by
    refine Finset.Subset.antisymm
      (Finset.union_subset (Finset.filter_subset _ _) (Finset.filter_subset _ _)) fun q hq => ?_
    rcases ht01 q hq with h | h
    · exact Finset.mem_union_left _ (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hq, h⟩)
    · exact Finset.mem_union_right _ (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hq, h⟩)
  refine ⟨t₁.image Prod.snd, t₀.image Prod.snd, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro y hy
    obtain ⟨q, hq, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 hy)
    exact mem_of_mem_liftPD_of_fst_eq_one
      (ht (Finset.mem_coe.2 (Finset.filter_subset _ _ hq))) (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2
  · intro y hy
    obtain ⟨q, hq, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 hy)
    exact mem_of_mem_liftPD_of_fst_eq_zero
      (ht (Finset.mem_coe.2 (Finset.filter_subset _ _ hq))) (Finset.mem_filter.1 hq).2
  · rw [Finset.card_image_of_injOn hinjOn₁, Finset.card_image_of_injOn hinjOn₀,
      ← Finset.card_union_of_disjoint hdisj, hunion]
  · ext q
    constructor
    · rintro (⟨y, hy, hyq⟩ | ⟨y, hy, hyq⟩)
      · have hyq' : ((1 : ℝ), y) = q := hyq
        obtain ⟨r, hr, hry⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 hy)
        have hqr : q = r := by rw [← hyq', ← hry]; exact heq₁ r hr
        exact Finset.mem_coe.2 (hqr ▸ Finset.filter_subset _ _ hr)
      · have hyq' : ((0 : ℝ), y) = q := hyq
        obtain ⟨r, hr, hry⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 (Finset.mem_coe.1 hy)
        have hqr : q = r := by rw [← hyq', ← hry]; exact heq₀ r hr
        exact Finset.mem_coe.2 (hqr ▸ Finset.filter_subset _ _ hr)
    · intro hq
      have hqt : q ∈ t := Finset.mem_coe.1 hq
      rcases ht01 q hqt with h1 | h0
      · have hq₁ : q ∈ t₁ := Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hqt, h1⟩
        have hqe : q = ((1 : ℝ), q.2) := (heq₁ q hq₁).symm
        rw [hqe]
        exact mem_liftPD_one (Finset.mem_coe.2 (Finset.mem_image.2 ⟨q, hq₁, rfl⟩))
      · have hq₀ : q ∈ t₀ := Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hqt, h0⟩
        have hqe : q = ((0 : ℝ), q.2) := (heq₀ q hq₀).symm
        rw [hqe]
        exact mem_liftPD_zero (Finset.mem_coe.2 (Finset.mem_image.2 ⟨q, hq₀, rfl⟩))

open scoped Pointwise

variable [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E]

/-- **The easy half of the homogenisation dictionary.** A point of `conv P + cone D`, lifted to
height `1`, lies in the pointed cone generated by the homogenisation `liftPD P D`. It is stated on
the unfolded `conv P + cone D` because `convexHullPD P D`, which is that expression by definition,
is introduced above this file; the converse half is `convexHullPD_eq_slice` there. -/
theorem lift_mem_coneHull_liftPD {P D : Set E} {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ convexHull ℝ P + (PointedCone.hull ℝ D : Set E)) :
    ((1 : ℝ), x) ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (liftPD P D) := by
  obtain ⟨u, hu, v, hv, rfl⟩ := hx
  have hpt : convexHull ℝ P ⊆ {w : E | ((1 : ℝ), w) ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (liftPD P D)} := by
    refine convexHull_min (fun y hy => PointedCone.subset_hull (mem_liftPD_one hy)) ?_
    intro y hy z hz a b ha hb hab
    have hsplit : ((1 : ℝ), a • y + b • z) = a • ((1 : ℝ), y) + b • ((1 : ℝ), z) := by
      refine Prod.ext ?_ rfl
      change (1 : ℝ) = a * 1 + b * 1
      rw [mul_one, mul_one, hab]
    change ((1 : ℝ), a • y + b • z) ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (liftPD P D)
    rw [hsplit]
    exact add_mem (Submodule.smul_mem _ (⟨a, ha⟩ : {c : ℝ // 0 ≤ c}) hy)
      (Submodule.smul_mem _ (⟨b, hb⟩ : {c : ℝ // 0 ≤ c}) hz)
  have hdir : ((0 : ℝ), v) ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (liftPD P D) := by
    obtain ⟨c, hcD, hc0, hcv⟩ := PointedCone.mem_hull_set.1 hv
    have hrepr : ((0 : ℝ), v) = ∑ y ∈ c.support, c y • (((0 : ℝ), y) : ℝ × E) := by
      refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
      · simp [Prod.fst_sum]
      · simpa [Prod.snd_sum, Finsupp.sum] using hcv.symm
    rw [hrepr]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun y hy => ?_
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ (⟨c y, hc0 y⟩ : {c : ℝ // 0 ≤ c})
      (PointedCone.subset_hull (mem_liftPD_zero (P := P) (hcD hy)))
  have hsplit : ((1 : ℝ), u + v) = ((1 : ℝ), u) + ((0 : ℝ), v) := by
    refine Prod.ext ?_ rfl
    change (1 : ℝ) = 1 + 0
    rw [add_zero]
  rw [hsplit]
  exact add_mem (hpt hu) hdir

/-- **Carathéodory for points and directions, in homogenised form.** A point of `conv P + cone D`
lifts to `(1, x)`, which is a positive combination of a *linearly independent* finite subset of the
homogenisation `liftPD P D`. This is the form the theorem is proved in and the only one that keeps
the linear independence. -/
theorem exists_linearIndepOn_subset_liftPD {P D : Set E} {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ convexHull ℝ P + (PointedCone.hull ℝ D : Set E)) :
    ∃ (t : Finset (ℝ × E)) (w : ℝ × E → ℝ), ↑t ⊆ liftPD P D ∧ (∀ q ∈ t, 0 < w q) ∧
      LinearIndepOn ℝ id (↑t : Set (ℝ × E)) ∧ ∑ q ∈ t, w q • q = ((1 : ℝ), x) :=
  exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_coneHull (lift_mem_coneHull_liftPD hx)

end LiftPD

section PointsDirections

open scoped Pointwise

variable {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]

/-- **Carathéodory for points and directions.** A point of `conv P + cone D` is a convex
combination of points of `P` plus a non-negative combination of directions of `D`, using **at most
`n + 1` generators in total**, `n = dim E`, all with strictly positive coefficients, and the
generators so obtained are **independent**: their homogenisation `liftPD ↑p ↑d` is linearly
independent in `ℝ × E`.

The proof homogenises to `ℝ × E`, where `conv P + cone D` is the level-one slice of the cone
generated by `{1} × P ∪ {0} × D`, and applies the conical Carathéodory theorem there. Linear
independence in `ℝ × E` is what produces the bound `n + 1`, and the first coordinate is what makes
the point weights sum to `1`. The independence clause is what the simplex form of the theorem
needs, and it is not recoverable from `exists_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull`. -/
theorem exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull {P D : Set E} {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ convexHull ℝ P + (PointedCone.hull ℝ D : Set E)) :
    ∃ (p d : Finset E) (a b : E → ℝ), ↑p ⊆ P ∧ ↑d ⊆ D ∧
      (∀ y ∈ p, 0 < a y) ∧ (∀ y ∈ d, 0 < b y) ∧ ∑ y ∈ p, a y = 1 ∧
      p.card + d.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 ∧
      LinearIndepOn ℝ id (liftPD (↑p : Set E) (↑d : Set E)) ∧
      (∑ y ∈ p, a y • y) + ∑ y ∈ d, b y • y = x := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨t, w, hts, hw, hli, hsum⟩ := exists_linearIndepOn_subset_liftPD hx
  -- the total number of generators is bounded by `dim (ℝ × E) = n + 1`
  have hcard : t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 := by
    have h := LinearIndependent.finset_card_le_finrank hli
    rwa [Module.finrank_prod, Module.finrank_self, add_comm] at h
  -- split `t` by height into points and directions
  obtain ⟨p, d, hpP, hdD, hcardpd, hlift⟩ := exists_finset_liftPD_eq hts
  -- read the splitting back as an identity of `Finset`s, which is what transports the weights
  have hinj₁ : Set.InjOn (fun y : E => ((1 : ℝ), y)) (↑p : Set E) :=
    fun _ _ _ _ h => congrArg Prod.snd h
  have hinj₀ : Set.InjOn (fun y : E => ((0 : ℝ), y)) (↑d : Set E) :=
    fun _ _ _ _ h => congrArg Prod.snd h
  have hteq : p.image (fun y : E => ((1 : ℝ), y)) ∪ d.image (fun y : E => ((0 : ℝ), y)) = t :=
    Finset.coe_injective <| by
      rw [Finset.coe_union, Finset.coe_image, Finset.coe_image]
      exact hlift
  have hdisj : Disjoint (p.image (fun y : E => ((1 : ℝ), y)))
      (d.image (fun y : E => ((0 : ℝ), y))) := by
    rw [Finset.disjoint_left]
    intro q hq hq'
    obtain ⟨y, -, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 hq
    obtain ⟨y', -, hy'⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 hq'
    exact absurd hy' (by simp)
  have hsplitR : ∀ f : ℝ × E → ℝ,
      ∑ q ∈ t, f q = (∑ y ∈ p, f ((1 : ℝ), y)) + ∑ y ∈ d, f ((0 : ℝ), y) := fun f => by
    rw [← hteq, Finset.sum_union hdisj, Finset.sum_image hinj₁, Finset.sum_image hinj₀]
  have hsplitE : ∀ f : ℝ × E → E,
      ∑ q ∈ t, f q = (∑ y ∈ p, f ((1 : ℝ), y)) + ∑ y ∈ d, f ((0 : ℝ), y) := fun f => by
    rw [← hteq, Finset.sum_union hdisj, Finset.sum_image hinj₁, Finset.sum_image hinj₀]
  have hmem₁ : ∀ y ∈ p, ((1 : ℝ), y) ∈ t := fun y hy => by
    have h := mem_liftPD_one (D := (↑d : Set E)) (Finset.mem_coe.2 hy)
    rw [hlift] at h
    exact Finset.mem_coe.1 h
  have hmem₀ : ∀ y ∈ d, ((0 : ℝ), y) ∈ t := fun y hy => by
    have h := mem_liftPD_zero (P := (↑p : Set E)) (Finset.mem_coe.2 hy)
    rw [hlift] at h
    exact Finset.mem_coe.1 h
  refine ⟨p, d, fun y => w ((1 : ℝ), y), fun y => w ((0 : ℝ), y), hpP, hdD,
    fun y hy => hw _ (hmem₁ y hy), fun y hy => hw _ (hmem₀ y hy), ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · -- the first coordinate of the conical identity makes the point weights sum to `1`
    have hfst : ∑ q ∈ t, w q * q.1 = 1 := by
      simpa [Prod.fst_sum, Prod.smul_fst, smul_eq_mul] using congrArg Prod.fst hsum
    rw [hsplitR fun q => w q * q.1] at hfst
    simpa using hfst
  · rw [hcardpd]
    exact hcard
  · rw [hlift]
    exact hli
  · -- the second coordinate is the point itself
    have hsnd : ∑ q ∈ t, w q • q.2 = x := by
      simpa [Prod.snd_sum, Prod.smul_snd] using congrArg Prod.snd hsum
    rw [hsplitE fun q => w q • q.2] at hsnd
    simpa using hsnd

/-- **Carathéodory for points and directions**, with the independence of the generators
forgotten. This is the form most consumers want;
`exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull` keeps the independence as well. -/
theorem exists_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull {P D : Set E} {x : E}
    (hx : x ∈ convexHull ℝ P + (PointedCone.hull ℝ D : Set E)) :
    ∃ (p d : Finset E) (a b : E → ℝ), ↑p ⊆ P ∧ ↑d ⊆ D ∧
      (∀ y ∈ p, 0 < a y) ∧ (∀ y ∈ d, 0 < b y) ∧ ∑ y ∈ p, a y = 1 ∧
      p.card + d.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 ∧
      (∑ y ∈ p, a y • y) + ∑ y ∈ d, b y • y = x := by
  obtain ⟨p, d, a, b, hp, hd, ha, hb, hsum, hcard, -, hval⟩ :=
    exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_convexHull_add_coneHull hx
  exact ⟨p, d, a, b, hp, hd, ha, hb, hsum, hcard, hval⟩

end PointsDirections


/-! ### Generators drawn from distinct members of a family

Corollaries 17.1.1–17.1.3 all sharpen Carathéodory's theorem by insisting that the generators come
from *different* members of a family. The whole content is the elimination step below, run on an
**index set** rather than on a set of vectors: a representation `x = ∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i` indexed by
`t : Finset ι` already carries at most one generator per index, so no coalescing is needed after
the fact. -/

section Indexed

variable {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E] {ι : Type*}

/-- The elimination step behind Corollaries 17.1.1–17.1.3, run on an index set and carrying a real
cost `c` that is not allowed to increase. `hpick` is the only place the conical and the affine
applications differ: it asks that every non-trivial dependency among the `v i` be normalisable so
that some coefficient is positive *and* the cost does not increase. For a conical representation
the cost is `0` and only the sign matters; for an affine one the coefficients sum to zero, so a
positive coefficient is automatic and the sign may be chosen by the cost. -/
private theorem exists_subset_linearIndepOn_aux (v : ι → E) (c : ι → ℝ)
    (hpick : ∀ (s : Finset ι) (mu : ι → ℝ), (∑ i ∈ s, mu i • v i = 0) → (∃ i ∈ s, mu i ≠ 0) →
      ∃ nu : ι → ℝ, (∑ i ∈ s, nu i • v i = 0) ∧ (∃ i ∈ s, 0 < nu i) ∧
        0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, nu i * c i) :
    ∀ (n : ℕ) (t : Finset ι), t.card ≤ n → ∀ w : ι → ℝ, (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) →
      ∃ (t₂ : Finset ι) (w₂ : ι → ℝ), t₂ ⊆ t ∧ (∀ i ∈ t₂, 0 < w₂ i) ∧
        LinearIndepOn ℝ v (t₂ : Set ι) ∧
        ∑ i ∈ t₂, w₂ i • v i = ∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i ∧
        ∑ i ∈ t₂, w₂ i * c i ≤ ∑ i ∈ t, w i * c i := by
  classical
  intro n
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    intro t hcard w hw
    have ht : t = (∅ : Finset ι) := Finset.card_eq_zero.1 (Nat.le_zero.1 hcard)
    subst ht
    refine ⟨∅, w, Finset.Subset.refl _, by simp, ?_, rfl, le_rfl⟩
    simp
  | succ n ih =>
    intro t hcard w hw
    by_cases hli : LinearIndepOn ℝ v (t : Set ι)
    · exact ⟨t, w, Finset.Subset.refl _, hw, hli, rfl, le_rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨fr, hfsupp, hfsum, hfne⟩ := linearDepOn_iff.1 hli
    rw [Finsupp.mem_supported] at hfsupp
    have hsub : fr.support ⊆ t := fun i hi => by exact_mod_cast hfsupp hi
    have hfrt : ∑ i ∈ t, fr i • v i = 0 := by
      rw [← Finset.sum_subset hsub fun i _ hi => by
        rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.1 hi, zero_smul]]
      exact hfsum
    obtain ⟨i₂, hi₂⟩ := Finsupp.support_nonempty_iff.2 hfne
    obtain ⟨mu, hmusum, ⟨y₀, hy₀t, hy₀pos⟩, hmuc⟩ :=
      hpick t (fun i => fr i) hfrt ⟨i₂, hsub hi₂, Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hi₂⟩
    set Pos : Finset ι := t.filter (fun i => 0 < mu i) with hPosdef
    have hPosne : Pos.Nonempty := ⟨y₀, by simp [hPosdef, hy₀t, hy₀pos]⟩
    obtain ⟨y₁, hy₁Pos, hy₁min⟩ := Finset.exists_min_image Pos (fun i => w i / mu i) hPosne
    have hy₁t : y₁ ∈ t := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hy₁Pos).1
    have hy₁mu : 0 < mu y₁ := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hy₁Pos).2
    set lam : ℝ := w y₁ / mu y₁ with hlamdef
    have hlampos : 0 < lam := div_pos (hw y₁ hy₁t) hy₁mu
    set w₂ : ι → ℝ := fun i => w i - lam * mu i with hw₂def
    have hw₂nonneg : ∀ i ∈ t, 0 ≤ w₂ i := by
      intro i hi
      by_cases hmi : 0 < mu i
      · have hmem : i ∈ Pos := by simp [hPosdef, hi, hmi]
        have hmul : lam * mu i ≤ w i := (le_div_iff₀ hmi).1 (hy₁min i hmem)
        simp only [hw₂def]
        linarith
      · push Not at hmi
        have hle : lam * mu i ≤ 0 := mul_nonpos_of_nonneg_of_nonpos hlampos.le hmi
        have hwi := hw i hi
        simp only [hw₂def]
        linarith
    have hw₂y₁ : w₂ y₁ = 0 := by
      simp only [hw₂def, hlamdef]
      rw [div_mul_cancel₀ _ hy₁mu.ne']
      ring
    have hsumv : ∑ i ∈ t, w₂ i • v i = ∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i := by
      have hsplit : ∑ i ∈ t, w₂ i • v i = (∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i) - lam • ∑ i ∈ t, mu i • v i := by
        rw [Finset.smul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
        simp only [hw₂def, sub_smul, smul_smul]
      rw [hsplit, hmusum, smul_zero, sub_zero]
    have hsumc : ∑ i ∈ t, w₂ i * c i ≤ ∑ i ∈ t, w i * c i := by
      have hsplit : ∑ i ∈ t, w₂ i * c i
          = (∑ i ∈ t, w i * c i) - lam * ∑ i ∈ t, mu i * c i := by
        rw [Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_sub_distrib]
        refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
        simp only [hw₂def]
        ring
      have hnn : 0 ≤ lam * ∑ i ∈ t, mu i * c i := mul_nonneg hlampos.le hmuc
      rw [hsplit]
      linarith
    set t₂ : Finset ι := t.filter (fun i => 0 < w₂ i) with ht₂def
    have ht₂sub : t₂ ⊆ t := Finset.filter_subset _ _
    have ht₂pos : ∀ i ∈ t₂, 0 < w₂ i := fun i hi => (Finset.mem_filter.1 hi).2
    have hzero : ∀ i ∈ t, i ∉ t₂ → w₂ i = 0 := by
      intro i hi hi₂
      have hnp : ¬ (0 < w₂ i) := fun h => hi₂ (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hi, h⟩)
      exact le_antisymm (not_lt.1 hnp) (hw₂nonneg i hi)
    have ht₂sumv : ∑ i ∈ t₂, w₂ i • v i = ∑ i ∈ t, w₂ i • v i :=
      Finset.sum_subset ht₂sub fun i hi hi₂ => by rw [hzero i hi hi₂, zero_smul]
    have ht₂sumc : ∑ i ∈ t₂, w₂ i * c i = ∑ i ∈ t, w₂ i * c i :=
      Finset.sum_subset ht₂sub fun i hi hi₂ => by rw [hzero i hi hi₂, zero_mul]
    have hy₁notin : y₁ ∉ t₂ := by simp [ht₂def, hw₂y₁]
    have ht₂card : t₂.card ≤ n := by
      have hss : t₂ ⊆ t.erase y₁ := fun i hi =>
        Finset.mem_erase.2 ⟨fun h => hy₁notin (h ▸ hi), ht₂sub hi⟩
      have h1 := Finset.card_le_card hss
      rw [Finset.card_erase_of_mem hy₁t] at h1
      have h2 : 0 < t.card := Finset.card_pos.2 ⟨y₁, hy₁t⟩
      omega
    obtain ⟨t₃, w₃, ht₃sub, ht₃pos, ht₃li, ht₃v, ht₃c⟩ := ih t₂ ht₂card w₂ ht₂pos
    refine ⟨t₃, w₃, ht₃sub.trans ht₂sub, ht₃pos, ht₃li, ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [ht₃v, ht₂sumv, hsumv]
    · exact le_trans (le_trans ht₃c (le_of_eq ht₂sumc)) hsumc

/-- A family of reals summing to zero over a `Finset`, not identically zero there, has a strictly
positive member. This is what makes the sign of an *affine* dependency free to choose. -/
theorem exists_pos_of_sum_eq_zero {s : Finset ι} {g : ι → ℝ} (hsum : ∑ i ∈ s, g i = 0)
    (hne : ∃ i ∈ s, g i ≠ 0) : ∃ i ∈ s, 0 < g i := by
  by_contra hcon
  push Not at hcon
  obtain ⟨i, his, hi⟩ := hne
  exact hi ((Finset.sum_eq_zero_iff_of_nonpos fun j hj => hcon j hj).1 hsum i his)

/-- **Carathéodory's elimination, indexed, conical form.** A non-negative combination
`∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i` is thinned to a sub-*index set* on which the `v i` are linearly independent,
keeping the value and strict positivity of the coefficients. Because the index set only shrinks, at
most one generator is used per index — the "each belonging to a different `Cᵢ`" clause of the
union form. -/
theorem exists_subset_linearIndepOn_of_sum (v : ι → E) (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ)
    (hw : ∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) :
    ∃ (t' : Finset ι) (w' : ι → ℝ), t' ⊆ t ∧ (∀ i ∈ t', 0 < w' i) ∧
      LinearIndepOn ℝ v (t' : Set ι) ∧ ∑ i ∈ t', w' i • v i = ∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i := by
  have hpick : ∀ (s : Finset ι) (mu : ι → ℝ), (∑ i ∈ s, mu i • v i = 0) →
      (∃ i ∈ s, mu i ≠ 0) → ∃ nu : ι → ℝ, (∑ i ∈ s, nu i • v i = 0) ∧ (∃ i ∈ s, 0 < nu i) ∧
        0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, nu i * (0 : ℝ) := by
    rintro s mu hsum ⟨i₀, hi₀s, hi₀⟩
    rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne hi₀ with hneg | hpos
    · refine ⟨fun i => -mu i, ?_, ⟨i₀, hi₀s, by linarith⟩, by simp⟩
      simp only [neg_smul, Finset.sum_neg_distrib, hsum, neg_zero]
    · exact ⟨mu, hsum, ⟨i₀, hi₀s, hpos⟩, by simp⟩
  obtain ⟨t', w', hsub, hpos, hli, hv, -⟩ :=
    exists_subset_linearIndepOn_aux v (fun _ => (0 : ℝ)) hpick t.card t le_rfl w hw
  exact ⟨t', w', hsub, hpos, hli, hv⟩

/-- Linear independence over an index set bounds the size of the index set by the dimension. -/
theorem card_le_finrank_of_linearIndepOn [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {v : ι → E} {t : Finset ι}
    (h : LinearIndepOn ℝ v (t : Set ι)) : t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E := by
  have hfin : Fintype ((t : Set ι) : Type _) := FinsetCoe.fintype t
  have h₁ := LinearIndependent.fintype_card_le_finrank h
  simpa using h₁

/-- A linearly independent lift `i ↦ (1, p i)` is an affinely independent family `i ↦ p i`. This is
the standard homogenisation, read on an index set. -/
theorem affineIndependent_of_linearIndepOn_one {p : ι → E} {s : Set ι}
    (h : LinearIndepOn ℝ (fun i => ((1 : ℝ), p i)) s) :
    AffineIndependent ℝ fun i : s => p (i : ι) := by
  rw [affineIndependent_iff]
  intro u g hg0 hgp e he
  refine linearIndependent_iff'.1 h u g ?_ e he
  refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
  · rw [Prod.fst_sum]
    simpa using hg0
  · rw [Prod.snd_sum]
    simpa using hgp

/-- **Carathéodory's elimination, indexed, affine form, with a cost.** A convex combination
`∑ i ∈ t, w i • p i` can be thinned to a sub-index set on which the `p i` are *affinely*
independent, keeping the value, the total weight and strict positivity, and without increasing the
cost `∑ i ∈ t, w i * c i`. The cost is what makes this the engine of the function form: with
`c i = fᵢ(pᵢ)` it says thinning never makes the convex-hull value worse. The sign of an affine
dependency may be chosen freely because its coefficients sum to zero. -/
theorem exists_subset_affineIndependent_of_sum (p : ι → E) (c : ι → ℝ) (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ)
    (hw : ∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) :
    ∃ (t' : Finset ι) (w' : ι → ℝ), t' ⊆ t ∧ (∀ i ∈ t', 0 < w' i) ∧
      AffineIndependent ℝ (fun i : (t' : Set ι) => p (i : ι)) ∧
      ∑ i ∈ t', w' i = ∑ i ∈ t, w i ∧
      ∑ i ∈ t', w' i • p i = ∑ i ∈ t, w i • p i ∧
      ∑ i ∈ t', w' i * c i ≤ ∑ i ∈ t, w i * c i := by
  have hpick : ∀ (s : Finset ι) (mu : ι → ℝ), (∑ i ∈ s, mu i • ((1 : ℝ), p i) = 0) →
      (∃ i ∈ s, mu i ≠ 0) →
      ∃ nu : ι → ℝ, (∑ i ∈ s, nu i • ((1 : ℝ), p i) = 0) ∧ (∃ i ∈ s, 0 < nu i) ∧
        0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, nu i * c i := by
    rintro s mu hsum hne
    have hone : ∑ i ∈ s, mu i = 0 := by
      have h₁ := congrArg Prod.fst hsum
      rw [Prod.fst_sum] at h₁
      simpa using h₁
    by_cases hc0 : 0 ≤ ∑ i ∈ s, mu i * c i
    · exact ⟨mu, hsum, exists_pos_of_sum_eq_zero hone hne, hc0⟩
    · refine ⟨fun i => -mu i, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
      · simp only [neg_smul, Finset.sum_neg_distrib, hsum, neg_zero]
      · refine exists_pos_of_sum_eq_zero ?_ ?_
        · simp only [Finset.sum_neg_distrib, hone, neg_zero]
        · obtain ⟨i, his, hi⟩ := hne
          exact ⟨i, his, by simpa using hi⟩
      · have : ∑ i ∈ s, -mu i * c i = -∑ i ∈ s, mu i * c i := by
          rw [← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => by ring
        rw [this]
        linarith [not_le.1 hc0]
  obtain ⟨t', w', hsub, hpos, hli, hv, hc⟩ :=
    exists_subset_linearIndepOn_aux (fun i => ((1 : ℝ), p i)) c hpick t.card t le_rfl w hw
  refine ⟨t', w', hsub, hpos, affineIndependent_of_linearIndepOn_one hli, ?_, ?_, hc⟩
  · have h₁ := congrArg Prod.fst hv
    rw [Prod.fst_sum, Prod.fst_sum] at h₁
    simpa using h₁
  · have h₂ := congrArg Prod.snd hv
    rw [Prod.snd_sum, Prod.snd_sum] at h₂
    simpa using h₂

/-- Affine independence over an index set bounds the size of the index set by `n + 1`. -/
theorem card_le_finrank_succ_of_affineIndependent [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {p : ι → E}
    {t : Finset ι} (h : AffineIndependent ℝ fun i : (t : Set ι) => p (i : ι)) :
    t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 := by
  have hfin : Fintype ((t : Set ι) : Type _) := FinsetCoe.fintype t
  have h₁ := h.card_le_finrank_succ (k := ℝ)
  have h₂ : Module.finrank ℝ (vectorSpan ℝ (Set.range fun i : (t : Set ι) => p (i : ι)))
      ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E := Submodule.finrank_le _
  have h₃ : Fintype.card ((t : Set ι) : Type _) = t.card := by simp
  omega

/-- **Coalescing** — Rockafellar's step "if two of the points with non-zero coefficients belong to
the same `Cᵢ`, the corresponding term can be coalesced". A positive combination of points each
drawn from some member of a family of convex sets is rewritten with one point per index, by
replacing the points from a single `C i` by their center of mass. -/
theorem exists_coalesced_sum {C : ι → Set E} (hC : ∀ i, Convex ℝ (C i)) {κ : Type*}
    (s : Finset κ) (w : κ → ℝ) (z : κ → E) (σ : κ → ι)
    (hw : ∀ j ∈ s, 0 < w j) (hz : ∀ j ∈ s, z j ∈ C (σ j)) :
    ∃ (t : Finset ι) (W : ι → ℝ) (Q : ι → E), (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < W i) ∧ (∀ i ∈ t, Q i ∈ C i) ∧
      ∑ i ∈ t, W i = ∑ j ∈ s, w j ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, W i • Q i = ∑ j ∈ s, w j • z j := by
  classical
  have hmaps : ∀ j ∈ s, σ j ∈ s.image σ := fun j hj => Finset.mem_image_of_mem σ hj
  have hWpos : ∀ i ∈ s.image σ, 0 < ∑ j ∈ s with σ j = i, w j := by
    intro i hi
    obtain ⟨j, hj, rfl⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 hi
    exact Finset.sum_pos (fun k hk => hw k (Finset.mem_filter.1 hk).1)
      ⟨j, Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hj, rfl⟩⟩
  refine ⟨s.image σ, fun i => ∑ j ∈ s with σ j = i, w j,
    fun i => (s.filter fun j => σ j = i).centerMass w z, hWpos, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro i hi
    refine Convex.centerMass_mem (hC i) (fun j hj => (hw j (Finset.mem_filter.1 hj).1).le)
      (hWpos i hi) fun j hj => ?_
    obtain ⟨hj₁, hj₂⟩ := Finset.mem_filter.1 hj
    exact hj₂ ▸ hz j hj₁
  · exact Finset.sum_fiberwise_of_maps_to hmaps w
  · have hstep : ∀ i ∈ s.image σ,
        (∑ j ∈ s with σ j = i, w j) • (s.filter fun j => σ j = i).centerMass w z
          = ∑ j ∈ s with σ j = i, w j • z j := by
      intro i hi
      rw [Finset.centerMass, smul_inv_smul₀ (hWpos i hi).ne']
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl hstep, Finset.sum_fiberwise_of_maps_to hmaps fun j => w j • z j]

/-- **Every vector of the convex cone generated by a union of convex sets `Cᵢ` is a non-negative
combination of at most `n` linearly independent vectors, each drawn from a different `Cᵢ`.** The
usual statement restricts to non-zero vectors and non-empty `Cᵢ`; neither is needed, since `t = ∅`
covers the origin and an empty `Cᵢ` never contributes an index. -/
theorem exists_linearIndepOn_of_mem_coneHull_iUnion [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {C : ι → Set E}
    (hC : ∀ i, Convex ℝ (C i)) {x : E} (hx : x ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (⋃ i, C i)) :
    ∃ (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ) (v : ι → E), (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) ∧ (∀ i ∈ t, v i ∈ C i) ∧
      LinearIndepOn ℝ v (t : Set ι) ∧ t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E ∧
      ∑ i ∈ t, w i • v i = x := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨c, hcs, hc0, hcx⟩ := PointedCone.mem_hull_set.1 hx
  have hsum : ∑ y ∈ c.support, c y • y = x := hcx
  rcases Finset.eq_empty_or_nonempty c.support with hsup | ⟨y₀, hy₀⟩
  · refine ⟨∅, fun _ => 0, fun _ => 0, by simp, by simp, by simp, by simp, ?_⟩
    rw [Finset.sum_empty, ← hsum, hsup, Finset.sum_empty]
  · have hchoice : ∀ y : E, ∃ i : ι, y ∈ c.support → y ∈ C i := by
      intro y
      by_cases hy : y ∈ c.support
      · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 (hcs (by exact_mod_cast hy))
        exact ⟨i, fun _ => hi⟩
      · obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 (hcs (by exact_mod_cast hy₀))
        exact ⟨i₀, fun h => absurd h hy⟩
    choose σ hσ using hchoice
    have hpos : ∀ y ∈ c.support, 0 < c y := fun y hy =>
      lt_of_le_of_ne (hc0 y) (Ne.symm (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.1 hy))
    obtain ⟨t, W, Q, hWpos, hQmem, -, hQsum⟩ :=
      exists_coalesced_sum hC c.support c id σ hpos fun y hy => hσ y hy
    obtain ⟨t', W', hsub, hpos', hli, hval⟩ := exists_subset_linearIndepOn_of_sum Q t W hWpos
    exact ⟨t', W', Q, hpos', fun i hi => hQmem i (hsub hi), hli,
      card_le_finrank_of_linearIndepOn hli, by rw [hval, hQsum]; simpa using hsum⟩

/-- **Every point of the convex hull of a union of convex sets `Cᵢ` is a convex combination of at
most `n + 1` affinely independent points, each drawn from a different `Cᵢ`.** -/
theorem exists_affineIndependent_of_mem_convexHull_iUnion [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {C : ι → Set E}
    (hC : ∀ i, Convex ℝ (C i)) {x : E} (hx : x ∈ convexHull ℝ (⋃ i, C i)) :
    ∃ (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ) (p : ι → E), (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, w i = 1 ∧
      (∀ i ∈ t, p i ∈ C i) ∧ AffineIndependent ℝ (fun i : (t : Set ι) => p (i : ι)) ∧
      t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, w i • p i = x := by
  classical
  rw [convexHull_eq] at hx
  obtain ⟨κ, s, w, z, hw₀, hw₁, hz, hcm⟩ := hx
  set s' : Finset κ := s.filter (fun j => 0 < w j) with hs'def
  have hsub : s' ⊆ s := Finset.filter_subset _ _
  have hwpos : ∀ j ∈ s', 0 < w j := fun j hj => (Finset.mem_filter.1 hj).2
  have hzero : ∀ j ∈ s, j ∉ s' → w j = 0 := by
    intro j hj hj'
    rcases eq_or_lt_of_le (hw₀ j hj) with h | h
    · exact h.symm
    · exact absurd (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hj, h⟩) hj'
  have hw₁' : ∑ j ∈ s', w j = 1 := by rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub hzero]; exact hw₁
  have hcm' : ∑ j ∈ s', w j • z j = x := by
    rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub fun j hj hj' => by rw [hzero j hj hj', zero_smul],
      ← Finset.centerMass_eq_of_sum_1 _ _ hw₁]
    exact hcm
  obtain ⟨j₀, hj₀⟩ : s'.Nonempty :=
    Finset.nonempty_of_sum_ne_zero (by rw [hw₁']; exact one_ne_zero)
  have hchoice : ∀ j : κ, ∃ i : ι, j ∈ s' → z j ∈ C i := by
    intro j
    by_cases hj : j ∈ s'
    · obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 (hz j (hsub hj))
      exact ⟨i, fun _ => hi⟩
    · obtain ⟨i₀, hi₀⟩ := Set.mem_iUnion.1 (hz j₀ (hsub hj₀))
      exact ⟨i₀, fun h => absurd h hj⟩
  choose σ hσ using hchoice
  obtain ⟨t, W, Q, hWpos, hQmem, hWsum, hQsum⟩ :=
    exists_coalesced_sum hC s' w z σ hwpos fun j hj => hσ j hj
  obtain ⟨t', W', hsub', hpos', hai, hone, hval, -⟩ :=
    exists_subset_affineIndependent_of_sum Q (fun _ => (0 : ℝ)) t W hWpos
  refine ⟨t', W', Q, hpos', by rw [hone, hWsum, hw₁'], fun i hi => hQmem i (hsub' hi), hai,
    card_le_finrank_succ_of_affineIndependent hai, by rw [hval, hQsum, hcm']⟩

end Indexed

/-! ### Carathéodory for the convex hull of a family of functions -/

section ConvFn

variable {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] {ι : Type*}

/-- **Any value strictly above `(conv {fᵢ})(x)` is already achieved by a convex combination in
which at most `n + 1` coefficients are non-zero**, one point per index, and the points carrying a
non-zero coefficient are affinely independent. The infimum defining `convFn` already produces one
point per index; the thinning to an affinely independent family is
`exists_subset_affineIndependent_of_sum` with cost `c i = fᵢ(pᵢ)`. The classical proof passes to a
"minimal `α'`" on the vertical line through `x`, a step that would not be available when
`conv {fᵢ}` is improper and is not needed here. -/
theorem exists_affineIndependent_of_convFn_lt {f : ι → E → EReal} (hf : ∀ i, ConvexFn (f i))
    (hf' : ∀ i x, f i x ≠ ⊥) {x : E} {r : ℝ} (h : convFn f x < (r : EReal)) :
    ∃ (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ) (p : ι → E), (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, w i = 1 ∧
      t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 ∧
      AffineIndependent ℝ (fun i : (t : Set ι) => p (i : ι)) ∧ (∀ i ∈ t, f i (p i) ≠ ⊤) ∧
      ∑ i ∈ t, w i • p i = x ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i) < (r : EReal) := by
  classical
  rw [convFn_apply hf hf'] at h
  obtain ⟨z, ⟨t, w, p, hw₀, hw₁, hwx, rfl⟩, hlt⟩ := sInf_lt_iff.1 h
  -- discard the indices carrying zero weight
  set t₁ : Finset ι := t.filter (fun i => 0 < w i) with ht₁def
  have hsub : t₁ ⊆ t := Finset.filter_subset _ _
  have hwpos : ∀ i ∈ t₁, 0 < w i := fun i hi => (Finset.mem_filter.1 hi).2
  have hzero : ∀ i ∈ t, i ∉ t₁ → w i = 0 := by
    intro i hi hi'
    rcases eq_or_lt_of_le (hw₀ i hi) with h₀ | h₀
    · exact h₀.symm
    · exact absurd (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hi, h₀⟩) hi'
  have hw₁' : ∑ i ∈ t₁, w i = 1 := by rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub hzero]; exact hw₁
  have hwx' : ∑ i ∈ t₁, w i • p i = x := by
    rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub fun i hi hi' => by rw [hzero i hi hi', zero_smul]]; exact hwx
  have hval : ∑ i ∈ t₁, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i) = ∑ i ∈ t, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i) := by
    refine Finset.sum_subset hsub fun i hi hi' => ?_
    rw [hzero i hi hi', EReal.coe_zero, zero_mul]
  -- on the surviving indices every term is finite
  have hbot : ∀ i ∈ t₁, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i) ≠ ⊥ := fun i hi =>
    EReal.coe_mul_ne_bot (hwpos i hi).le (hf' i (p i))
  have htop : ∑ i ∈ t₁, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i) ≠ ⊤ := by
    rw [hval]
    exact (hlt.trans (EReal.coe_lt_top r)).ne
  have hnetop := EReal.forall_ne_top_of_sum_ne_top t₁ _ hbot htop
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ : ∃ c : ι → ℝ, ∀ i ∈ t₁, f i (p i) = (c i : EReal) := by
    refine ⟨fun i => (f i (p i)).toReal, fun i hi => ?_⟩
    have hne : f i (p i) ≠ ⊤ := fun hcon =>
      hnetop i hi (by rw [hcon, EReal.coe_mul_top_of_pos (hwpos i hi)])
    exact (EReal.coe_toReal hne (hf' i (p i))).symm
  have hreal : ∀ (u : Finset ι), u ⊆ t₁ → ∀ v : ι → ℝ,
      ∑ i ∈ u, (v i : EReal) * f i (p i) = ((∑ i ∈ u, v i * c i : ℝ) : EReal) := by
    intro u hu v
    rw [EReal.coe_sum]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => by
      rw [hc i (hu hi), ← EReal.coe_mul]
  -- thin the representation to an affinely independent one, without increasing the cost
  obtain ⟨t', w', hsub', hpos', hai, hone, hpt, hcost⟩ :=
    exists_subset_affineIndependent_of_sum p c t₁ w hwpos
  refine ⟨t', w', p, hpos', by rw [hone, hw₁'], card_le_finrank_succ_of_affineIndependent hai,
    hai, fun i hi => by rw [hc i (hsub' hi)]; exact EReal.coe_ne_top _,
    by rw [hpt, hwx'], ?_⟩
  rw [hreal t' hsub' w']
  refine lt_of_le_of_lt (EReal.coe_le_coe_iff.2 hcost) ?_
  rw [← hreal t₁ (Finset.Subset.refl _) w, hval]
  exact hlt

/-- **The convex hull of a family of convex functions is computed by the defining infimum
restricted to convex combinations in which at most `n + 1` coefficients are non-zero** and the
corresponding points are affinely independent. -/
theorem convFn_apply_affineIndependent {f : ι → E → EReal} (hf : ∀ i, ConvexFn (f i))
    (hf' : ∀ i x, f i x ≠ ⊥) (x : E) :
    convFn f x = sInf {z : EReal | ∃ (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ) (p : ι → E),
      (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, w i = 1 ∧ t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 ∧
        AffineIndependent ℝ (fun i : (t : Set ι) => p (i : ι)) ∧ (∀ i ∈ t, f i (p i) ≠ ⊤) ∧
        ∑ i ∈ t, w i • p i = x ∧ z = ∑ i ∈ t, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i)} := by
  refine le_antisymm (le_sInf ?_) ?_
  · rintro z ⟨t, w, p, hpos, hone, -, -, -, hpt, rfl⟩
    rw [convFn_apply hf hf']
    exact sInf_le ⟨t, w, p, fun i hi => (hpos i hi).le, hone, hpt, rfl⟩
  · by_contra hcon
    rw [not_le] at hcon
    obtain ⟨r, hr₁, hr₂⟩ := EReal.lt_iff_exists_real_btwn.1 hcon
    obtain ⟨t, w, p, hpos, hone, hcard, hai, hnetop, hpt, hlt⟩ :=
      exists_affineIndependent_of_convFn_lt hf hf' hr₁
    have hmem : (∑ i ∈ t, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i)) ∈
        {z : EReal | ∃ (t : Finset ι) (w : ι → ℝ) (p : ι → E),
          (∀ i ∈ t, 0 < w i) ∧ ∑ i ∈ t, w i = 1 ∧ t.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 ∧
            AffineIndependent ℝ (fun i : (t : Set ι) => p (i : ι)) ∧ (∀ i ∈ t, f i (p i) ≠ ⊤) ∧
            ∑ i ∈ t, w i • p i = x ∧ z = ∑ i ∈ t, (w i : EReal) * f i (p i)} :=
      ⟨t, w, p, hpos, hone, hcard, hai, hnetop, hpt, rfl⟩
    exact absurd (sInf_le hmem) (not_le.2 (hlt.trans hr₂))

end ConvFn

/-! ### Carathéodory for the convex hull of a single function -/

section ConvHullFn

variable {E : Type*} [AddCommGroup E] [Module ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]

/-- The padding step: a sum over a `Finset` of size at most `N` becomes a sum
over the *fixed* index type `Fin N` once the surplus indices are given a zero summand. `jj` is any
enumeration of the `Finset` by `Fin N` that is faithful on the first `t.card` indices. -/
private theorem sum_pad_eq {M : Type*} [AddCommMonoid M] {κ : Type*} (t : Finset κ) {N : ℕ}
    (hcard : t.card ≤ N) (jj : Fin N → κ)
    (hjj : ∀ j : Fin t.card, jj (Fin.castLE hcard j) = (t.equivFin.symm j : κ)) (H : κ → M) :
    ∑ i : Fin N, (if (i : ℕ) < t.card then H (jj i) else 0) = ∑ j ∈ t, H j := by
  classical
  rw [sum_ite_lt hcard fun i => H (jj i),
    Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => by rw [hjj j],
    Fintype.sum_equiv t.equivFin.symm _ (fun y : {y // y ∈ t} => H (y : κ)) fun _ => rfl,
    Finset.sum_coe_sort t H]

/-- **For an arbitrary function `g` never taking the value `-∞`, the convex hull `conv g` is
computed by convex combinations of exactly `n + 1` points**:
`(conv g)(x) = inf {∑_{i<n+1} λᵢ g(xᵢ) | ∑ λᵢ xᵢ = x, ∑ λᵢ = 1, λᵢ ≥ 0}`. No convexity is assumed,
and the points need not be distinct — repetitions and zero coefficients turn "at most `n + 1`
points" into a statement about the fixed index `Fin (n + 1)`, the convention `0 · (+∞) = 0` making
a zero coefficient harmless. Carathéodory applied to `epi g` would give `n + 2` points; the
reduction to `n + 1` is the elimination run on the *base* points with the vertical coordinate as
its cost. -/
theorem convHullFn_apply_fin {g : E → EReal} (hg : ∀ x, g x ≠ ⊥) (x : E) :
    convHullFn g x = sInf {z : EReal |
      ∃ (w : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ) (p : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E),
        (∀ i, 0 ≤ w i) ∧ ∑ i, w i = 1 ∧ ∑ i, w i • p i = x ∧
          z = ∑ i, (w i : EReal) * g (p i)} := by
  classical
  rw [convHullFn]
  refine le_antisymm (le_sInf ?_) ?_
  -- **`≤`**: the hull is below the value of every `n + 1`-point representation.
  · rintro z ⟨w, p, hw₀, hw₁, hwx, rfl⟩
    by_cases htop : ∑ i, (w i : EReal) * g (p i) = ⊤
    · rw [htop]; exact le_top
    have hbot : ∀ i ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1))),
        (w i : EReal) * g (p i) ≠ ⊥ := fun i _ => EReal.coe_mul_ne_bot (hw₀ i) (hg (p i))
    have hnetop := EReal.forall_ne_top_of_sum_ne_top Finset.univ _ hbot htop
    set t' : Finset (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1)) :=
      Finset.univ.filter (fun i => 0 < w i) with ht'def
    have hsub : t' ⊆ Finset.univ := Finset.subset_univ _
    have hzero : ∀ i ∈ (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1))),
        i ∉ t' → w i = 0 := by
      intro i _ hi'
      rcases eq_or_lt_of_le (hw₀ i) with h | h
      · exact h.symm
      · exact absurd (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨Finset.mem_univ i, h⟩) hi'
    have hw₁' : ∑ i ∈ t', w i = 1 := by rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub hzero]; exact hw₁
    have hwx' : ∑ i ∈ t', w i • p i = x := by
      rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub fun i hi hi' => by rw [hzero i hi hi', zero_smul]]; exact hwx
    obtain ⟨μ, hμ⟩ : ∃ μ : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ,
        ∀ i ∈ t', g (p i) = (μ i : EReal) := by
      refine ⟨fun i => (g (p i)).toReal, fun i hi => ?_⟩
      have hpos : 0 < w i := (Finset.mem_filter.1 hi).2
      have hne : g (p i) ≠ ⊤ := fun hcon =>
        hnetop i (Finset.mem_univ i) (by rw [hcon, EReal.coe_mul_top_of_pos hpos])
      exact (EReal.coe_toReal hne (hg (p i))).symm
    have hcm := Finset.centerMass_mem_convexHull t'
      (fun i hi => ((Finset.mem_filter.1 hi).2).le) (by rw [hw₁']; exact zero_lt_one)
      (z := fun i => ((p i, μ i) : E × ℝ))
      (fun i hi => mk_mem_epi.2 (le_of_eq (hμ i hi)))
    rw [Finset.centerMass_eq_of_sum_1 _ _ hw₁'] at hcm
    have hsplit : ∑ i ∈ t', w i • ((p i, μ i) : E × ℝ) = (x, ∑ i ∈ t', w i * μ i) := by
      refine Prod.ext ?_ ?_
      · rw [Prod.fst_sum]; simpa using hwx'
      · rw [Prod.snd_sum]; simp [smul_eq_mul]
    rw [hsplit] at hcm
    refine (ofEpi_apply_le hcm).trans (le_of_eq ?_)
    rw [EReal.coe_sum,
      ← Finset.sum_subset hsub (fun i hi hi' => by rw [hzero i hi hi']; simp)]
    exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => by rw [hμ i hi, ← EReal.coe_mul]
  -- **`≥`**: every point of the hull of `epi g` admits an `n + 1`-point representation.
  · refine le_ofEpi fun ν hν => ?_
    rw [convexHull_eq] at hν
    obtain ⟨κ, s, w, zz, hw₀, hw₁, hzz, hcm⟩ := hν
    set s' : Finset κ := s.filter (fun j => 0 < w j) with hs'def
    have hsub : s' ⊆ s := Finset.filter_subset _ _
    have hwpos : ∀ j ∈ s', 0 < w j := fun j hj => (Finset.mem_filter.1 hj).2
    have hzero : ∀ j ∈ s, j ∉ s' → w j = 0 := by
      intro j hj hj'
      rcases eq_or_lt_of_le (hw₀ j hj) with h | h
      · exact h.symm
      · exact absurd (Finset.mem_filter.2 ⟨hj, h⟩) hj'
    have hw₁' : ∑ j ∈ s', w j = 1 := by rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub hzero]; exact hw₁
    have hcm' : ∑ j ∈ s', w j • zz j = (x, ν) := by
      rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub fun j hj hj' => by rw [hzero j hj hj', zero_smul],
        ← Finset.centerMass_eq_of_sum_1 _ _ hw₁]
      exact hcm
    have hx : ∑ j ∈ s', w j • (zz j).1 = x := by
      have h := congrArg Prod.fst hcm'
      rw [Prod.fst_sum] at h
      simpa using h
    have hnu : ∑ j ∈ s', w j * (zz j).2 = ν := by
      have h := congrArg Prod.snd hcm'
      rw [Prod.snd_sum] at h
      simpa [smul_eq_mul] using h
    obtain ⟨t', w', hsubt, hpos', hai, hsum1, hsumx, hsumc⟩ :=
      exists_subset_affineIndependent_of_sum (fun j => (zz j).1) (fun j => (zz j).2) s' w hwpos
    rw [hw₁'] at hsum1
    rw [hx] at hsumx
    rw [hnu] at hsumc
    have hcard : t'.card ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E + 1 :=
      card_le_finrank_succ_of_affineIndependent (p := fun j => (zz j).1) hai
    have htne : t'.Nonempty := by
      rw [Finset.nonempty_iff_ne_empty]
      intro hcon
      rw [hcon, Finset.sum_empty] at hsum1
      exact zero_ne_one hsum1
    have hm0 : 0 < t'.card := Finset.card_pos.2 htne
    set r : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → Fin t'.card :=
      fun i => ⟨min (i : ℕ) (t'.card - 1), by omega⟩ with hrdef
    set jj : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → κ := fun i => (t'.equivFin.symm (r i) : κ) with hjjdef
    have hrj : ∀ j : Fin t'.card, r (Fin.castLE hcard j) = j := by
      intro j
      have hj := j.2
      refine Fin.ext ?_
      simp only [hrdef, Fin.val_castLE]
      omega
    have hjj : ∀ j : Fin t'.card, jj (Fin.castLE hcard j) = (t'.equivFin.symm j : κ) := by
      intro j
      simp only [hjjdef, hrj j]
    have hmemt : ∀ i, jj i ∈ t' := fun i => (t'.equivFin.symm (r i)).2
    set W : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ :=
      fun i => if (i : ℕ) < t'.card then w' (jj i) else 0 with hWdef
    set P : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E := fun i => (zz (jj i)).1 with hPdef
    have hW0 : ∀ i, 0 ≤ W i := by
      intro i
      simp only [hWdef]
      split
      · exact (hpos' _ (hmemt i)).le
      · exact le_rfl
    have hWsum : ∑ i, W i = 1 := by
      rw [hWdef, sum_pad_eq t' hcard jj hjj w']
      exact hsum1
    have hWx : ∑ i, W i • P i = x := by
      have hterm : ∀ i, W i • P i =
          if (i : ℕ) < t'.card then (fun j => w' j • (zz j).1) (jj i) else 0 := by
        intro i
        simp only [hWdef, hPdef]
        split <;> simp
      rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => hterm i,
        sum_pad_eq t' hcard jj hjj fun j => w' j • (zz j).1]
      exact hsumx
    have hWE : ∑ i, (W i : EReal) * g (P i) = ∑ j ∈ t', (w' j : EReal) * g ((zz j).1) := by
      have hterm : ∀ i, (W i : EReal) * g (P i) =
          if (i : ℕ) < t'.card then (fun j => (w' j : EReal) * g ((zz j).1)) (jj i) else 0 := by
        intro i
        simp only [hWdef, hPdef]
        split
        · rfl
        · rw [EReal.coe_zero, zero_mul]
      rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => hterm i,
        sum_pad_eq t' hcard jj hjj fun j => (w' j : EReal) * g ((zz j).1)]
    have hmem : (∑ i, (W i : EReal) * g (P i)) ∈ {z : EReal |
        ∃ (w : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → ℝ) (p : Fin (Module.finrank ℝ E + 1) → E),
          (∀ i, 0 ≤ w i) ∧ ∑ i, w i = 1 ∧ ∑ i, w i • p i = x ∧
            z = ∑ i, (w i : EReal) * g (p i)} := ⟨W, P, hW0, hWsum, hWx, rfl⟩
    refine le_trans (sInf_le hmem) ?_
    rw [hWE]
    calc ∑ j ∈ t', (w' j : EReal) * g ((zz j).1)
        ≤ ∑ j ∈ t', (w' j : EReal) * (((zz j).2 : ℝ) : EReal) := by
          refine Finset.sum_le_sum fun j hj => ?_
          exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left (hzz j (hsub (hsubt hj)))
            (by exact_mod_cast (hpos' j hj).le)
      _ = ((∑ j ∈ t', w' j * (zz j).2 : ℝ) : EReal) := by
          rw [EReal.coe_sum]
          exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j _ => EReal.coe_mul _ _
      _ ≤ (ν : EReal) := by exact_mod_cast hsumc

end ConvHullFn




/-! ### Which half-spaces contain an intersection of half-spaces

`inequalitySet B S` is the solution set of the system `⟪x, y⟫ ≤ μ`, one inequality per
`(y, μ) ∈ S`. A closed half-space `{x | ⟪x, y₀⟫ ≤ μ₀}` contains it as soon as `(y₀, μ₀)` lies in the
convex cone generated by `S` together with `(0, 1)`; the converse holds when that cone is closed,
which happens as soon as `S` is compact and misses the origin. -/

section HalfSpace

variable {E F : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
  [NormedAddCommGroup F] [NormedSpace ℝ F] [FiniteDimensional ℝ F]

/-- The solution set of the system of linear inequalities `⟪x, y⟫ ≤ μ` indexed by `(y, μ) ∈ S`:
an arbitrary intersection of closed half-spaces of `E`. -/
def inequalitySet (B : E →ₗ[ℝ] F →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ) (S : Set (F × ℝ)) : Set E :=
  {x | ∀ q ∈ S, B x q.1 ≤ q.2}

variable {B : E →ₗ[ℝ] F →ₗ[ℝ] ℝ} {S : Set (F × ℝ)}

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] in
theorem mem_inequalitySet {x : E} : x ∈ inequalitySet B S ↔ ∀ q ∈ S, B x q.1 ≤ q.2 := Iff.rfl

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] in
/-- A non-negative combination of the given inequalities, with the right-hand side weakened at
will, is again valid on the solution set. This half of the representation theorem asks nothing of
`S`. -/
theorem inequalitySet_subset_halfSpace_of_mem_coneHull {y₀ : F} {μ₀ : ℝ}
    (h : ((y₀, μ₀) : F × ℝ) ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (insert ((0 : F), (1 : ℝ)) S)) :
    inequalitySet B S ⊆ {x : E | B x y₀ ≤ μ₀} := by
  intro x hx
  have hcone : ∀ q ∈ PointedCone.hull ℝ (insert ((0 : F), (1 : ℝ)) S), B x q.1 ≤ q.2 := by
    intro q hq
    induction hq using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem q hq =>
        rcases hq with rfl | hq
        · simp
        · exact hx q hq
    | zero => simp
    | add a b _ _ ha hb =>
        have hadd : B x (a + b).1 = B x a.1 + B x b.1 := by
          rw [Prod.fst_add, map_add]
        rw [hadd, Prod.snd_add]
        exact add_le_add ha hb
    | smul c a _ ha =>
        have hc : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (c : ℝ) := c.2
        have hfst : B x (c • a).1 = (c : ℝ) * B x a.1 := by
          change B x ((c : ℝ) • a.1) = (c : ℝ) * B x a.1
          rw [map_smul, smul_eq_mul]
        have hsnd : ((c • a).2 : ℝ) = (c : ℝ) * a.2 := rfl
        rw [hfst, hsnd]
        exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ha hc
  exact hcone _ h

omit [FiniteDimensional ℝ F] in
/-- A compatible pairing separates the points of its second space, so a non-zero `y` is moved by
some `⟪·, y⟫`. -/
private theorem exists_pairing_ne_zero [IsCompatiblePairing B.flip] {y : F} (hy : y ≠ 0) :
    ∃ x : E, B x y ≠ 0 := by
  by_contra hcon
  push Not at hcon
  refine hy (SeparatingDual.eq_zero_of_forall_dual_eq_zero (R := ℝ) fun g => ?_)
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := exists_pairing_eq B.flip g
  rw [hx y]
  exact hcon x

